<div><figure class="my-4 flex flex-col"><!-- -2 children --></figure><p><!-- -1 children --></p><p>The first round of qualifying for the 110th Indianapolis 500 was rained out Saturday, leading to a busy, condensed schedule on Sunday.</p><p>Storms and showers rained out practice on Saturday morning and kept coming into the afternoon, forcing IndyCar to push all qualifying to Sunday.</p><div class="flex items-center">
        
      <!-- -1 children --></div><p><!-- -1 children --></p><p>Qualifying will begin at noon on Sunday, and each driver will only get one try at qualifying for the Fast 12 and a second qualifying session. More on this procedure can be found . <!-- -1 children --></p><p>Fortunately for IndyCar, Sunday's activities at Indianapolis Motor Speedway won't be rained out. Forecasters are calling for a dry, warm and mostly sunny day on Sunday.</p><figure class="my-4 flex flex-col"><!-- -1 children --></figure><p>The green flag will drop on the iconic race at 12:45 p.m. on May 24.</p></div>


